menu "Audio engine"

config AUDIO_SCRATCH_ENABLED
    bool "Enable vinyl/scratch mode (jog platter scratches the audio)"
    default n
    help
        When enabled, touching the FLX4 jog platter top while a deck plays
        scratches the audio (forward + reverse) by driving a read head over the
        per-deck PSRAM scratch capture buffer, instead of the Phase 1 platter
        hold+scrub. Releasing seeks normal forward playback to the head position.
        Additive: with this off the output path is unchanged and touching the
        platter does the Phase 1 hold/scrub. See docs/VINYL_SCRATCH_PLAN.md.

config AUDIO_PCM_TIMELINE_QUALIFICATION
    bool "Run one-shot PCM timeline hardware qualification"
    default n
    help
        Test-build-only gate. On boot, run 100 forced low-word wrap and
        playhead handoff repetitions with a higher-priority same-core reader,
        then measure both unhooked publications for 100 repetitions. The
        result is written as TIMELINE_QUALIFICATION in the service journal.
        Keep this disabled in production and release-candidate images.

endmenu
